# Keep the developer's machine out of the image.
#
# The Dockerfile does `COPY . .`, and Vite reads .env.local in EVERY mode, production included. A
# `.env.local` holding VITE_PUBLIC_BASE=http://localhost:5173 -- which is exactly what the local dev
# server needs -- was reaching the build and baking that address into the production bundle. Every
# shareable link the app produced (task link, file share, meeting invite) pointed at a laptop.
#
# Git does not protect against this: .env.local is gitignored, but the deploy tars the working
# directory, not the git tree. So the exclusion has to live here as well.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.tauri
.env.development
.env.production

node_modules
dist
src-tauri/target
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.turbo
